ard, special nutritional programs, social services, recreational activities, entertainment, and other services. The Standard Bearer segment leases post-acute care properties to healthcare operators. In addition, the company operates senior living units; and provides ancillary services consisting of digital x-ray, ultrasound, electrocardiograms, sub-acute services, dialysis, respiratory, and long-term care pharmacy and patient transportation to people in their homes or at long-term care facilities, as well as mobile diagnostics. The company operates healthcare facilities in Alabama, Alaska, Arizona, Colorado, Idaho, Iowa, Kansas, Oregon, Nebraska, Nevada, South Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Washington, and Wisconsin. The company was incorporated in 1999 and is based in San Juan Capistrano, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Barry R. Port | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 51 | Compensation: $10.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 46K people. Revenue per employee of $110K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 15%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 99\u00d7 revenue per employee (high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["The Ensign Group, Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $10.3B market cap on $5.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 53\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 53% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5282351560034092},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"News sentiment running negative (-0.13) across recent coverage","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","18 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (20.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The Ensign Group, Inc. Sued for Securities Law Violations - Contact the DJS Law Group to Discuss Your Rights - ENSG","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/the-ensign-group-inc-sued-for-securities-law-violations---contact-the-djs-law-group-to-discuss-your-rights--ensg-302946065.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795121820.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ENSG Investors Have Opportunity to Lead The Ensign Group, Inc. Securities Fraud Lawsuit with SBS Law","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/ensg-investors-have-opportunity-to-lead-the-ensign-group-inc-securities-fraud-lawsuit-with-sbs-law-302946064.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795121760.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"INVESTOR ALERT: Pomerantz Law Firm Reminds Investors with Losses on their Investment in The Ensign Group, Inc. of Class Action Lawsuit and Upcoming Deadlines - ENSG","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/investor-alert-pomerantz-law-firm-reminds-investors-with-losses-on-their-investment-in-the-ensign-group-inc-of-class-action-lawsuit-and-upcoming-deadlines--ensg-302944846.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795100400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.375,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"ENSG Loss Alert: Ensign Group Investors Sued for Securities Fraud in Connection with 8% Stock Drop and Alleged Misrepresentations about its Neglect Issues","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/ne